.git
.env
passwords.json
# Runtime/secret files: never baked into the image (availability.json is
# regenerated by the watchdog on boot; calendar.json and vault.json hold the
# owner's private data). The REST of data/ (clinicas.json, photos.json, the
# sprite atlas) IS baked — those are the build-time base assets the app ships
# with. /app/data is a PERSISTENT VOLUME at runtime (docker-compose.yml mounts
# app_data:/app/data; Coolify must configure a persistent storage path the same
# way), which SHADOWS this baked data/ and is where install-owned packs
# (data/packs) and the canonical install config (turnos.env) live durably —
# see docs/architecture/deploy.md. Baking the base assets here is how they
# reach a first boot; the volume is how everything written afterwards survives.
data/availability.json
data/watch.json
data/watch-state.json
data/vault.json
data/calendar.json
data/doctor-photo-batches/
logs/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
*.pyc
.playwright-mcp/
docs/*.png
verify-*.png
design-handoff/
